-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008), §67 שינוי בשכר המנהל כתוצאה מרמת מורכבות בית
-- הספר: a change in the school's own complexity changes the principal's
-- pay — a rise to the new level's combined salary; a fall by the
-- complexity supplement, he being taken to have banked 10% of each year's
-- supplement from his first year there, the new supplement the banked sum
-- and (100% − 10% × his years there) of the new level's supplement; and
-- the clause's two worked examples.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `base-agreement-common`
IMPORT conventions

§ `67 שינוי בשכר המנהל כתוצאה מרמת מורכבות בית הספר`

-- (א): only a change in the school itself, not one caused by other
-- schools' changes alone, changes the pay.
@ref akn:art_67__para_a
GIVEN `the change comes from the school itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change of level changes the principal's pay` `the change comes from the school itself` IF
    `the change comes from the school itself`

-- (ב): on a rise, the combined salary of the new level (from the
-- principals' table, an input).
@ref akn:art_67__para_b
GIVEN `the new level's combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's combined salary after a rise` `the new level's combined salary` IS
    `the new level's combined salary`

-- (ג): on a fall, the complexity supplement changes; ¶2: the supplement is
-- the principal's combined salary less a level-1 principal's of the same
-- grade.
@ref akn:art_67__para_c akn:art_67__para_c/p2
GIVEN `combined salary at the level` IS A NUMBER, `combined salary at level 1, same grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity supplement` `combined salary at the level` `combined salary at level 1, same grade` IS
    `combined salary at the level` MINUS `combined salary at level 1, same grade`

-- (ד): the supplement after a fall is (1) the sum banked, 10% of each
-- year's supplement from the first year in the school, plus (2) [100% −
-- 10% × years in the school] × the new level's supplement.
-- F-ofek-hadash-base-67-a: nothing stops the years at ten. From the
-- eleventh year (2) is below nothing and (1) passes the supplement the
-- principal had: after twelve years at level 3 and a fall to level 2, the
-- formula gives more than the level-3 supplement he had before the fall.
-- The reading adopted: the years count up to ten, so the banked share
-- reaches 100% and (2) is never below nothing.
@ref akn:art_67__para_d akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2/p3
GIVEN `supplement in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement after a fall, as printed` `supplement in each year so far` `the new level's supplement` IS
        sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD 10% TIMES s) `supplement in each year so far`)
    PLUS (100% MINUS 10% TIMES count `supplement in each year so far`) TIMES `the new level's supplement`

GIVEN `supplement in each year so far` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the new level's supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement after a fall` `supplement in each year so far` `the new level's supplement` IS
    `the supplement after a fall, as printed` (take 10 `supplement in each year so far`) `the new level's supplement`

-- The examples (cls_1, cls_2), on the supplements they print: 2,436 at
-- level 3, 1,218 at level 2, none at level 1.
@ref akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2__cls_1 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2__cls_1/p2 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2__cls_2 akn:art_67__para_d__subpara_2__cls_2/p2
`four years at level 3` MEANS LIST 2436, 2436, 2436, 2436

-- (1): 4 × 10% × 2,436 + 60% × 1,218 = 1,705.2, printed 1,705.
#ASSERT `the supplement after a fall` `four years at level 3` 1218 EQUALS 1705.2
#ASSERT `to the nearest whole` (`the supplement after a fall` `four years at level 3` 1218) EQUALS 1705
-- (2): 4 × 10% × 2,436 + 2 × 10% × 1,218 + 40% × 0 = 1,218.
#ASSERT `the supplement after a fall` (append `four years at level 3` (LIST 1218, 1218)) 0 EQUALS 1218

-- F-ofek-hadash-base-67-a's evidence: twelve years at level 3, then level 2.
`twelve years at level 3` MEANS replicate 12 2436
`after twelve years a fall raises the supplement, as printed` MEANS
    `the supplement after a fall, as printed` `twelve years at level 3` 1218 GREATER THAN 2436
#ASSERT `after twelve years a fall raises the supplement, as printed`
#ASSERT `the supplement after a fall` `twelve years at level 3` 1218 EQUALS 2436

-- With the years at most ten, the supplement after a fall is never more
-- than the one before it, nor less than the new level's — over every span
-- of 1 to 15 years at level 3 falling to level 2.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD
                    `the supplement after a fall` (replicate n 2436) 1218 AT MOST 2436
                AND `the supplement after a fall` (replicate n 2436) 1218 AT LEAST 1218)
            (range 1 15)
